@page "/fold-parity"
@rendermode @(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))

@*
    Prerendering is off for this page specifically (see the remarks on FoldParityView.cs): with it on,
    the .NET HtmlRenderer would already write every container's markup verbatim into the first HTML
    response, and if the interactive circuit's first render batch matches that DOM exactly, Blazor
    applies no edits and the JS insertMarkup/insertText functions this test exists to exercise never run.
    Disabling prerendering here means the containers below are genuinely empty until the circuit
    connects and performs its first render, which is the only way this page's comparison can be of the
    browser-side path rather than of the same server-written HTML twice.
*@
<FoldParityView />
